translations={
'R001':('Cooling System Reliability','The main engine cooling water system shall provide high operational reliability. Inadequate cooling capacity, interruption of cooling water circulation or loss of temperature control shall not impair the safe operation of the propulsion plant. The system shall maintain stable cooling capacity during continuous operation, in high-temperature tropical waters and during changes in main engine load.'),
'ER-R001-01':('Pump Redundancy and Protection','The main engine cooling water system shall be equipped with at least two cooling water pumps, at least one of which shall be independently electrically driven. Each pump shall be capable of independently meeting the cooling water flow requirement at the rated power of the main engine. The system shall provide high-temperature alarms and automatic protection to prevent inadequate cooling capacity, interruption of cooling water circulation or loss of temperature control from impairing the safe operation of the propulsion plant.'),
'ER-R001-02':('Tropical Cooling Design Basis','The main engine cooling water system shall maintain stable cooling capacity in high-temperature tropical waters. The maximum seawater temperature used for system design shall be confirmed against the project Design Basis, and the cooling water temperature shall remain within the limits specified by the main engine manufacturer.'),
'ER-R001-03':('Load-Change Temperature Control','The main engine cooling water system shall be equipped with automatic temperature regulation that adjusts the cooling water temperature as the main engine load changes and maintains it within the limits specified by the main engine manufacturer. The system shall provide high-temperature alarms and automatic protection, and shall issue an alarm when the cooling water temperature exceeds the high-alarm setpoint.'),
'ER-R001-04':('Tropical Cooling Capacity','The system shall maintain stable cooling capacity in high-temperature tropical waters. Specific cooling capacity parameters shall be confirmed against the main engine manufacturer\'s Technical Data.'),
'R002':('Cooling Design Parameters','The cooling water temperature, pressure and flow at the main engine inlet and outlet shall meet the requirements of the main engine manufacturer\'s technical documentation. The design parameters of the high-temperature and low-temperature cooling water circuits shall be consistent with the main engine technical data, pump curves, cooler selection and heat-balance calculations.'),
'ER-R002-01':('Inlet Temperature Limits','The main engine cooling water system shall be designed to maintain the cooling water temperature at the engine inlet within the limits specified by the engine manufacturer. The difference between the maximum inlet temperature of the high-temperature fresh-water circuit and the thermostat opening temperature shall not exceed 36°C.'),
'ER-R002-01-01':('Low-Temperature Pressure Limit','The main engine cooling water pressure shall meet the requirements of the main engine manufacturer\'s technical documentation. The pressure in the low-temperature cooling water circuit shall not exceed 2 bar (based on the MAN 49/60 Project Guide; for other manufacturers, confirm against their Technical Data).'),
'ER-R002-01-02':('Cooling Water Flow Verification','The main engine cooling water flow shall meet the requirements of the main engine manufacturer\'s technical documentation and shall be verified through heat-balance calculations and pump curves.'),
'ER-R002-02':('HT and LT Parameter Consistency','The design parameters of the high-temperature and low-temperature cooling water circuits shall be consistent with the main engine technical data, pump curves, cooler selection and heat-balance calculations.'),
'R004':('Cooling System Installation','The cooling water system piping arrangement shall be clear, compact and suitable for construction. Pipe routing, valve locations, support arrangement, drain points, vent points and equipment interfaces shall facilitate on-site welding, installation, flushing, pressure testing and subsequent inspection.'),
'ER-R004-01':('Piping Installation Access','The cooling water system piping arrangement shall be clear and compact. Pipe routing shall facilitate on-site welding, installation, flushing, pressure testing and subsequent inspection.'),
'ER-R004-02':('Valve and Support Access','Valve locations and support arrangements shall facilitate on-site operation, installation and subsequent inspection. Sufficient space shall be provided on the valve operating side, and supports shall allow convenient fastening and adjustment.'),
'ER-R004-03':('Drain and Vent Locations','Drain points shall be provided at the lowest points of the piping and vent points at the highest points to facilitate system flushing and pressure testing.'),
'ER-R004-04':('Equipment Interface Access','Equipment interfaces shall facilitate on-site welding, installation and subsequent inspection. Sufficient working space shall be provided around the interfaces, with consideration given to ease of dismantling and maintenance.'),
}
